{
  "description": "The Responses streaming `error` event nests its failure under `error` \u2014 the wire is `{ \"type\": \"error\", \"error\": { \"type\", \"code\", \"message\", \"param\" }, \"sequence_number\" }` \u2014 but ResponseErrorEvent (and its beta twin BetaResponseErrorEvent) declare flat, required `code`/`message`/`param`, so the event fails to decode or decodes without its failure. Replace the flat members with the nested `error` object (`type` and `message` required; `code`/`param` optional and nullable). The docs only ever show one shape, so the flat members are removed rather than kept optional. Observed live on streamed POST /responses by alchemy's OpenAI LanguageModel, which carried a local decode workaround for it (2026-10).",
  "patches": [
    {
      "op": "remove",
      "path": "/components/schemas/ResponseErrorEvent/properties/code"
    },
    {
      "op": "remove",
      "path": "/components/schemas/ResponseErrorEvent/properties/message"
    },
    {
      "op": "remove",
      "path": "/components/schemas/ResponseErrorEvent/properties/param"
    },
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/components/schemas/ResponseErrorEvent/properties/error",
      "value": {
        "type": "object",
        "description": "The error that interrupted the stream.",
        "properties": {
          "type": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The error type, e.g. `invalid_request_error`."
          },
          "code": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "description": "The error code."
          },
          "message": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The error message."
          },
          "param": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "description": "The parameter the error relates to."
          }
        },
        "required": ["type", "message"]
      }
    },
    {
      "op": "replace",
      "path": "/components/schemas/ResponseErrorEvent/required",
      "value": ["type", "error", "sequence_number"]
    },
    {
      "op": "remove",
      "path": "/components/schemas/BetaResponseErrorEvent/properties/code"
    },
    {
      "op": "remove",
      "path": "/components/schemas/BetaResponseErrorEvent/properties/message"
    },
    {
      "op": "remove",
      "path": "/components/schemas/BetaResponseErrorEvent/properties/param"
    },
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/components/schemas/BetaResponseErrorEvent/properties/error",
      "value": {
        "type": "object",
        "description": "The error that interrupted the stream.",
        "properties": {
          "type": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The error type, e.g. `invalid_request_error`."
          },
          "code": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "description": "The error code."
          },
          "message": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The error message."
          },
          "param": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "description": "The parameter the error relates to."
          }
        },
        "required": ["type", "message"]
      }
    },
    {
      "op": "replace",
      "path": "/components/schemas/BetaResponseErrorEvent/required",
      "value": ["type", "error", "sequence_number"]
    }
  ]
}
